{
  "rules": [
    "Near-term (days 1–10): model is slightly low during rising regimes; apply a small upward bias (+0.2 to +0.8) when the last 5–10 days show positive momentum.",
    "Mid-horizon (days ~11–22): model tends to overpredict during pullbacks (too slow to price in dips); damp forecasts toward recent spot/short MA (shrink deviations from last price by ~10–20%).",
    "Late horizon (days ~23–30): model systematically underestimates breakout/rally tails (misses upside acceleration); add an upside tail adjustment (+2 to +8 by day 30) when trend + volatility are elevated.",
    "Turning points: forecasts are lagged/smoothed—underreact to sharp up-moves and overreact to subsequent mean reversion; use regime switch: if a new high occurs, reduce mean-reversion strength for ~1 week; if a sharp drop occurs, increase mean-reversion strength for ~1 week.",
    "After spikes/new highs: model often predicts reversion too early/too strongly; cap downward corrections and keep forecasts closer to the recent high until momentum fades (e.g., don’t project >1–2/day declines for the next ~5–7 days in strong uptrends)."
  ]
}
